<h2 class="bde-heading-506-128 bde-heading">
Why Is Jaxson Hayes on $6m in 2026-27?
</h2><div class="bde-fancy-container-506-129 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-fancy-container-506-145 bde-fancy-container">
  
  
	



<div class="bde-f-text-506-158 bde-f-text">
<p>Hayes is paid <strong>$6m</strong> because a lottery pick whose rookie contract ended without an extension spent three years on minimum deals before a club used an exception on him.</p>
<ul>
<li>He went eighth in 2019 and his rookie contract was worth <strong>$22.12m</strong>.</li>
<li>His qualifying offer was reduced because he did not meet the starter criteria.</li>
<li>The <a href="/teams/los-angeles-lakers/">Lakers</a> paid him <strong>$4.63m</strong> across two seasons at the minimum.</li>
<li>The new deal is <strong>$12m</strong> with <strong>$6m</strong> guaranteed.</li>
<li>At 7 foot he is one of three Utah players at that height or taller.</li>
</ul>
<p>His salary this season is more than his last two combined.</p>

