<script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jaxson-hayes/#faq","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://nbasalaries.com/players/jaxson-hayes/"},"mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jaxson Hayes’s 2026-27 Salary?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hayes earns $6m in 2026-27, level with Josh Okogie at Utah and the first year of a new two-year contract. It rises from $3.45m last season. His career earnings come to $36.2m across eight seasons. The salary is 3.28% of the club’s $182.97m payroll."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What’s Next for Jaxson Hayes Beyond 2026?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"One more season follows this one, a club option on 2027-28 with a June 29, 2027 deadline. Of the $12m total, $6m is guaranteed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How Much Does Jaxson Hayes Earn Over Time?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A $6m season is hard to picture, so here's what it comes to over smaller stretches of time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When Does Jaxson Hayes’s Contract Expire?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hayes signed a two-year contract worth $12m with Utah in 2026 using the mid-level exception, of which $6m is guaranteed. The second season is a club option with a June 29, 2027 deadline. He would reach free agency in 2028 at 28."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What Is Jaxson Hayes’s Net Worth?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hayes’s net worth is estimated at around $14.48m, taken from his $36.2m in career earnings. No outlet publishes a figure for him. He played one season at Texas and went eighth in the 2019 draft, a month after he turned 19."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why Is Jaxson Hayes on $6m in 2026-27?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Hayes is paid $6m because a lottery pick whose rookie contract ended without an extension spent three years on minimum deals before a club used an exception on him. His salary this season is more than his last two combined."}}]}</script>
